  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is zero evidence about which design choices matter. The most informative first step is to establish a clean, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is the simplest possible configuration: one modality, one profile, a well-established RNA encoder, and no aggregation or fusion to confound interpretation. This establishes a performance floor for RNA data and creates a clear anchor for all future comparisons: (a) does multiprofile + aggregation help (compare to config_002)? (b) does adding an image modality help (compare to config_029/034)? (c) does encoder choice matter (compare to config_013 or config_026)? Starting from the simplest configuration ensures that any future performance gains can be attributed to specific design additions rather than being entangled with multiple simultaneous changes. Under a limited budget, this single experiment maximizes the number of informative follow-up comparisons it enables."
}

